=== SIGNATURE ===
make_change(coins, price)

=== COMMENT ===
Greedy change: takes as many of the largest denomination as fit without exceeding price, then the next largest, and so on. coins is a vertical array of denominations; returns a matching array of counts. Prefers higher denominations even when a lower-denomination mix would land closer to the price.

=== CODE ===
=LAMBDA(coins, price, LET(
   cvec, TOCOL(coins),
   ncoins, ROWS(cvec),
   scale, 1000000,
   cnum, IFERROR(cvec * 1, 0),
   pnum, IFERROR(price * 1, 0),
   ds, IF(cnum > 0, ROUND(cnum * scale, 0), 0),
   ps, MAX(ROUND(pnum * scale, 0), 0),
   idx, SEQUENCE(ncoins),
   ord, SORTBY(idx, ds, -1),
   sorted_ds, SORTBY(ds, ds, -1),
   rem_after, SCAN(ps, sorted_ds, LAMBDA(rem, coin, IF(coin < 1, rem, MOD(rem, coin)))),
   rem_before, TAKE(VSTACK(ps, rem_after), ncoins),
   count_sorted, IF(sorted_ds < 1, 0, INT(rem_before / sorted_ds)),
   count_orig, SORTBY(count_sorted, ord),
   IF(ROWS(coins) >= COLUMNS(coins), count_orig, TRANSPOSE(count_orig))
))

=== DESCRIPTION ===
Makes change for a price by taking as many of the biggest coin as possible without going over, then the next biggest, and so on.

Arguments:
  coins - a vertical array of the coin denominations available (e.g. {1; 0.5; 0.25; 0.05}). Non-positive or non-numeric entries are treated as unusable and get a count of 0.
  price - the target amount. The result never exceeds it.

Returns:
  An array the same shape as coins giving how many of each denomination to use. It is a largest-first greedy: it does not minimise the number of coins or get as close to the price as theoretically possible - it just prefers higher denominations.

  Because of that it can leave more on the table than a different mix would - e.g. make_change({0.25; 0.10}, 0.30) returns {1; 0} (0.25), not {0; 3} (0.30), because one quarter uses the higher denomination even though three dimes would hit 0.30 exactly.

  The input order of coins does not matter - denominations are ranked by value internally and the counts are returned in the original positions.

Example:
  make_change({1; 0.5; 0.25; 0.05}, 4.34)  ->  {4; 0; 1; 1}   (4.30)
  make_change({0.25; 0.10}, 0.30)          ->  {1; 0}         (0.25)

Note: denominations and price are scaled to integers (six decimal places) so the greedy arithmetic is exact; no dynamic programming or helper lambdas are involved.
